  "title": "Clothes shopping",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "The future for 'I' ends in **-ব** (*-bo*): কেনা 'buy' → **কিনব** (*kinbo*) 'I will buy'. For আপনি it's **-বেন**: **কিনবেন** 'you will buy'. Put **না** after the verb to negate: **কিনব না** 'I won't buy'.\n\nUseful words: **শাড়ি** (sari), **জামা** (shirt / top / dress), **লুঙ্গি** (the wrap many Bangladeshi men wear at home). Colours go before the noun: **লাল শাড়ি** 'a red sari'.\n\nBefore paying with a big note, ask **ভাংতি আছে?** 'Do you have change?' — in Kolkata it's **খুচরো** (*khuchro*).\n\n**Culture:** red-and-white saris are the classic choice for Pohela Boishakh (Bengali New Year), which you'll meet in Unit 10.\n\n**ভাংতি** and **খুচরা** both mean \"change\" (small notes and coins) — you will hear both.",
